{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T12:48:14.613Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","call_id":"call_WB533qwR1Ymv5efqk8WO5xMA","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Usage: kompile [options] <file>\n  Options:\n    --backend <backend>\n      Choose a backend. <backend> is one of [llvm|haskell|kore]. Each creates \n      the kompiled K definition.\n      Default: llvm\n    --coverage\n      Generate coverage data when executing semantics.\n      Default: false\n    --debug\n      Print debugging output messages and error stack traces\n      Default: false\n    --debug-warnings\n      Print debugging output messages and error/warning stack traces\n      Default: false\n    --emit-json\n      Emit JSON serialized version of parsed and kompiled definitions.\n      Default: false\n    --enable-llvm-debug\n      Enable debugging support for the LLVM backend.\n      Default: false\n    --enable-search\n      By default, to reduce compilation time, `krun --search` is disabled on \n      the LLVM backend. Pass this flag to enable it.\n      Default: false\n    --gen-bison-parser\n      Emit bison parser for the PGM configuration variable within the syntax \n      module of your definition into the kompiled definition.\n      Default: false\n    --gen-glr-bison-parser\n      Emit GLR bison parser for the PGM configuration variable within the \n      syntax module of your definition into the kompiled definition.\n      Default: false\n    --help, -h\n      Print this help message\n    --help-hidden, -hh\n      Print advanced options help message\n    --main-module <name>\n      Specify main module in which a program starts to execute. This \n      information is used by 'krun'. The default is the name of the given K \n      definition file without the extension (.k).\n    --md-selector <expression>\n      Preprocessor: for .md files, select only the md code blocks that match